0919 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420921 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420923 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420924 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420929 1075 #edb/ref 17592186420928 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420929 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420929 1077 "selection" 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420929 1078 #edb/ref 17592186420921 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420929 1079 #uuid "71f2f20d-59aa-5f4b-b243-cfacb310155a" 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420930 1068 #edb/ref 17592186420929 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420930 1069 "q-129741" 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420930 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420930 1071 "Let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}{e}^{y}.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-1,0).$" 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420930 1072 #uuid "55146915-2d47-5b59-9386-37303589ba19" 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420930 1074 "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y)≈f(a,b)+∇f(a,b)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(-1,0)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(-1,0)+∇f(-1,0)\\cdot ⟨x+1,y⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(-1,0)=1.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & =2x{e}^{y}\\, &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{x}(-1,0)=-2, \\\\ {f}_{y} & ={x}^{2}{e}^{y} &  & ⇒\\, & {f}_{y}(-1,0)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(-1,0)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-1,0) & =⟨-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & ≈f(-1,0)+∇f(-1,0)\\cdot ⟨x+1,y⟩ \\\\  & ≈1+⟨-2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨x+1,y⟩ \\\\  & ≈1-2(x+1)+y \\\\  & ≈-1-2x+y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420931 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420935 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420931 1062 #uuid "271dc584-8067-5c79-8663-42f0cf534fe1" 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420931 1063 #edb/ref 17592186362293 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420932 1062 #uuid "428b58fe-7d44-5904-bbbf-8158fe8c3758" 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420932 1063 #edb/ref 17592186420930 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420933 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420934 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420933 1062 #uuid "ac2d8892-990a-561c-b817-20d63c4e20b5" 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420933 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125007 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420934 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420931 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420934 1062 #uuid "de8e0d3a-aa28-5870-806b-fac6775a1e3e" 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420934 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125255 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420935 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420932 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420935 1062 #uuid "f9443769-9265-54cf-81f2-24a4db8a375c" 13194139534421 17592186045417 true] [17592186420935 1063 #edb/ref 17592186265764 13194139534421 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-e616bf48-afee-5693-88d5-4ed73b51c3cc" 17592186420918 "answer-19a5d7fe-a63b-5e32-949d-b3f2969e0db8" 17592186420919 "answer-3996a57d-3ca8-524e-b713-371dae9f92c2" 17592186420920 "answer-3a60a799-4271-555e-b402-ed7491785238" 17592186420921 "answer-783e5bf5-dd91-511c-81fe-eca19c21cfc0" 17592186420922 "answer-9c37dd2d-538f-57a0-aa67-b6fb35e4d8ed" 17592186420923 "answer-b8cdea38-23c3-571a-bf79-4dd2da2d05bc" 17592186420924 "answer-bb0f50fc-3f9e-56b0-874f-3d40ee14ed33" 17592186420925 "answer-df1e2f42-abc0-5025-a335-6ed1280fc719" 17592186420926 "answer-f7a0590c-c153-5bd3-ab0a-b20fc19d4881" 17592186420927 "answer-fe73bc79-5